WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.408
Hi! Today is about the family.

2
00:00:06.808 --> 00:00:11.256
Who is that? That's my mother!

3
00:00:12.967 --> 00:00:17.319
This is the family. Listen:

4
00:00:17.719 --> 00:00:19.839
the father

5
00:00:20.239 --> 00:00:22.335
the mother

6
00:00:22.735 --> 00:00:24.879
the brother

7
00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:27.471
the sister

8
00:00:27.871 --> 00:00:29.943
grandpa

9
00:00:30.343 --> 00:00:32.415
grandma

10
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.932
The verb haben (to have) is very important. Listen:

11
00:00:39.332 --> 00:00:41.932
I have a brother.

12
00:00:42.332 --> 00:00:44.404
Look:

13
00:00:44.804 --> 00:00:46.876
I have

14
00:00:47.276 --> 00:00:49.348
you have

15
00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:52.348
he has, she has

16
00:00:52.748 --> 00:00:54.820
we have

17
00:00:56.533 --> 00:01:01.701
Mein or meine? With der and das we say mein:

18
00:01:02.101 --> 00:01:05.301
my father, my child

19
00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.349
With die we say meine:

20
00:01:08.749 --> 00:01:12.189
my mother, my parents

21
00:01:12.589 --> 00:01:15.717
And dein and deine (your) work the same way.

22
00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:22.697
Listen: Lena and Mateo talk about family.

23
00:01:23.097 --> 00:01:25.625
Do you have siblings?

24
00:01:26.025 --> 00:01:29.177
Yes, I have a sister.

25
00:01:29.577 --> 00:01:32.465
What's your sister's name?

26
00:01:32.865 --> 00:01:36.617
Her name is Anna. And you?

27
00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:39.689
I have two brothers.

28
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:47.912
Now you! Do you have siblings? What's your mother's name?

29
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.736
Great! Now you can:

30
00:02:00.136 --> 00:02:06.744
You introduce your family. And you know haben and mein, meine.

31
00:02:07.144 --> 00:02:09.264
See you soon!
